			<section id="en" class="lang-section">
				<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
				<p class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdatedEn}</p>
				<p>Coheria is a guided breathing app, published by Nicolas Tardieu. This page describes, in plain words, the data the app uses, where it goes and how you stay in control. In short: everything stays on your phone, unless you create an account (backup), get Coheria Complete, as a subscription or a one-time purchase (payment), or agree to usage statistics (measurement). Nothing else leaves the device.</p>
				<article>
					<h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
					<p>Coheria is published by Nicolas Tardieu, an independent developer, who is the data controller. For any question: Settings › Write to the creator, or <a href="mailto:coheria.contact@gmail.com">coheria.contact@gmail.com</a>.</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h2>2. What stays on your phone</h2>
					<p>Without an account, everything Coheria records lives only on your device:</p>
					<ul>
						<li>your sessions (date, time, duration, session name), your streak and your freeze days;</li>
						<li>how you felt at the end of each session;</li>
						<li>your custom sessions and each session’s settings (duration, rhythm, sounds, vibrations);</li>
						<li>your preferences: theme, language, reminders, your answer about usage statistics;</li>
						<li>the state of your subscription or purchase.</li>
					</ul>
					<p>This data disappears when you uninstall the app, or with one tap in Settings › Account › Erase my data.</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h2>3. The account, optional</h2>
					<p>You can create an account with Google or Apple to keep your progress safe and find it again on another phone. Coheria never requires one.</p>
					<p>What the account holds: your email address, a technical identifier, the provider you used (Google or Apple) and the creation date. With Google, the account also keeps your name and the link to your profile picture, as Google sends them at sign-in; Coheria doesn’t use or display them anywhere. No password is asked for or stored. With Apple, you can hide your address: Coheria then receives a relay address.</p>
					<p>What is backed up: a copy of your streak, sessions, feelings, settings and reminders, updated on every change and attached to your account. Your answer about usage statistics stays specific to each phone.</p>
					<p>Where: sign-in and backup are provided by Supabase (Supabase Inc.), an authentication and database hosting provider. Google and Apple only receive the sign-in request. Supabase privacy policy: <a href="https://supabase.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">supabase.com/privacy</a>.</p>
					<p>Deleting: “Erase my data” removes the copy attached to the account. “Delete my account” deletes the account and its copy immediately. Both are in Settings › Account, two taps, no delay and no request to send.</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h2>4. Purchases</h2>
					<p>Coheria Complete is sold as a yearly subscription (with a trial period) or as a one-time lifetime purchase, through the App Store or Google Play. Payment is handled by Apple or Google: Coheria never sees your payment details.</p>
					<p>To verify the purchase and unlock Complete, Coheria relies on RevenueCat (RevenueCat Inc.), which receives an anonymous app identifier, the transaction identifier and the device type. “Restore purchase” re-reads your purchases from Apple or Google. RevenueCat privacy policy: <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">revenuecat.com/privacy</a>.</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h2>5. Usage statistics, with your consent</h2>
					<p>Coheria doesn’t ask right away whether it may measure its usage: the question comes later, on the home screen, once you know the app. Until then, the events described below stay on your phone and nothing is sent. If you agree, they are sent; if you decline, they are deleted at once; with no answer, each one is deleted after seven days. You can change your mind at any time in Settings › Usage statistics: withdrawing consent stops measurement immediately.</p>
					<p>If you agree, Coheria sends the events of its measurement plan: onboarding finished (the goal chosen out of three, whether you want a reminder, whether you start right away), session started, session completed (type and duration), feeling logged (the fact, never the answer), reminder added, changed or removed, answer to the notification permission, app opened from a notification, Complete offer shown, purchase. Along with them go the app being opened, sent to the background, installed or updated, and a few technical details: app version, phone model and system, language, time zone, screen size. The screens you visit are not tracked. Nothing about how you feel, no name, no address, no location.</p>
					<p>These measurements are processed by PostHog (PostHog Inc.) and hosted in the European Union, in Frankfurt. Coheria asks PostHog not to derive any location from your phone’s IP address. Each installation gets a random identifier. Measurements are never attached to your account or your email address, even if you have one. They are kept for 12 months, then deleted. PostHog privacy policy: <a href="https://posthog.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">posthog.com/privacy</a>.</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h2>6. Reminders</h2>
					<p>Reminders are local notifications, scheduled and managed on your phone. Nothing is sent to a server. You can turn them off in the app (Settings › Reminders) or in the phone settings.</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h2>7. What Coheria does not do</h2>
					<ul>
						<li>No advertising, no ad tracking, no cross-referencing with other apps.</li>
						<li>No health data read or written: Coheria uses neither Apple Health nor Google Fit.</li>
						<li>No location, no contacts, no microphone.</li>
						<li>No sale or transfer of data.</li>
					</ul>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h2>8. How long</h2>
					<ul>
						<li>On your phone: as long as the app is installed, or until “Erase my data”.</li>
						<li>On your account: until “Erase my data” or “Delete my account”.</li>
						<li>Usage statistics: 12 months.</li>
						<li>Purchases: transaction records are kept by Apple, Google and RevenueCat under their own rules and accounting obligations.</li>
					</ul>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h2>9. Your rights</h2>
					<p>Under the GDPR, you can access your data, correct it, erase it, retrieve it or object to a processing. In the app, everything is done without a request: erase or delete in Settings › Account, withdraw consent in Settings › Usage statistics. For a copy of your data or any other request, write to us from Settings › Write to the creator or at <a href="mailto:coheria.contact@gmail.com">coheria.contact@gmail.com</a>; we answer within 30 days. You can also lodge a complaint with your data protection authority (in France, the CNIL).</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h2>10. Security</h2>
					<p>Exchanges with the account, purchases and statistics go through encrypted connections. Access to your account relies on your Google or Apple session: Coheria holds no password. On the phone, data lives in the app’s private storage.</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h2>11. Changes</h2>
					<p>The date at the top of this page shows the last update. A previous version of the text can be requested by email.</p>
				</article>
			</section>

